# ==== T-FMT-B — SYNONYM: the SET literal's SECOND emit site (brief-review
# pass 6, blocking-grade).
# SCOPE CLAIM: `Expr::ArrayLiteral` has TWO bracket-emitting paths, and the
# spelling dispatch must patch both. The flat `doc::surround` path is the one
# everybody sees; when `has_interior_comments` fires, the arm instead routes
# through `format_bracketed_broken_with_comments("[", "]", …)`, which spells
# its own delimiters. A fix applied only to the flat path leaves this shape
# silently rewritten `{}` -> `[]` — and the corpus reparse gate is BLIND to it,
# because the rewritten output re-parses perfectly.
void main():
    Set[int] s = {
        # a leading interior comment forces the broken-with-comments path
        1,
        2,  # trailing
        3,
    }
    print(s.len())
